What is the Golden Star? The control you use to activate your Lucky Wish.
Does Lucky 7 bring out two tokens? Yes, when several of your tokens are in base. Each of the two 6s can bring one token out.
Can I use the Lucky Wish on any turn? Yes. You can use it on any turn, but only once per match.
Turn timer
Is there a turn timer? Yes, and it is optional. The room host chooses 60, 90 or 120 seconds, or turns it off.
What happens when the timer runs out? Your turn passes to the next player.
Can the turn timer be turned off? Yes. The room host can turn it off.
Who sets the turn timer? The room host.
The leader and strategy
Who is the leader? The player who is closest to winning.
Do AI opponents go after the leader? Yes. AI opponents are designed to hunt the leader.
Why do opponents sometimes place their tokens in front of each other? When a player is close to winning, trailing players may set up captures for each other. A capture gives a reroll, which can then be used to hit the leader.
How can I stop a leader? Hunt the leader’s tokens on the open track. Star squares and the coloured home path are safe, so only tokens on the open track can be captured.
How can I protect myself when I am the leader? Stop on star squares, move tokens in pairs where you can, and get tokens onto your coloured home path quickly.
Which capture should I choose when I have a choice? The leader’s token is usually the best target.
What is a good strategy for beginners? Bring tokens out when you roll a 6, check for captures before every move, use the safe places, and watch the leader. The Strategies page has more.
