10. Quick facts (single source of truth)
•	One-sentence description: Ludo Emperor 5 Way is a five-player, Ludo-style strategy game played with two dice, where the first player to get all four tokens onto their coloured home path wins.
•	Players and tokens: five players, four tokens each. Player colours: red, green, yellow, blue and orange.
•	Dice: two per turn. Use both on one token, or one on each of two tokens. If you have no legal move, the turn passes. Tokens and turns move clockwise.
•	Sixes: a single 6 brings a token out of base. Every 6 gives an extra turn, with no limit on how many in a row.
•	Capturing: landing on a lone opponent token on the open track sends it to base and gives you a reroll. It can be done with one die or the total.
•	Safe from capture: star squares, coloured home paths and base. A pair is safe from a single token.
•	Pairs: captured only when two opposing tokens land together, one with each die. Capturing a pair gives one reroll. A pair can be split freely.
•	Missed Capture Penalty: if you could capture and did not, the token that could have captured goes back to base. Rule 7 lists every case.
•	Centre home: reaching it needs an exact roll and gives an extra turn, but it is not needed to win.
•	Lucky 7: with no token on the open track, a total of 7 counts as 6+6 and gives an extra turn. Two tokens can come out of base.
•	Lucky Wish: two numbers chosen before the match, used once on any turn, 6 and 6 not allowed. A wish totalling 7 can trigger Lucky 7.
•	Turn timer: optional, set by the room host (60, 90, 120 seconds or off). When it runs out, the turn passes.
•	Extra turns come from: rolling a 6, a capture, moving a token into the centre home, and Lucky 7.
•	End of the match: the match ends as soon as a player wins. The other players are ranked by progress percentage.
•	Number of rules: 12.
•	Winning: all four tokens on the coloured home path, whether or not any reached the centre.
